# The request line and the rest of the format. Every request goes to httpbin.org, whose /anything echoes
# back the method, URL, headers and body it received, so the response shows what was sent. Needs a
# network connection.

### The method can be any case: this one is sent as GET
get https://httpbin.org/anything

### A custom method is sent as written (httpbin answers 405 Method Not Allowed: it got a PROPFIND)
PROPFIND https://httpbin.org/anything
Depth: 1

### A URL without a scheme gets http://
httpbin.org/anything?scheme=none

### A path alone takes its host from the Host header
GET /anything?from=host-header
Host: httpbin.org

### A long query continues on indented lines starting with ? or &
GET https://httpbin.org/anything
    ?search=keyboard driven editor
    &page=2
    &sort=stars

### HTTP/1.1 at the end of the line chooses the protocol (the response headers start with the version)
GET https://httpbin.org/anything HTTP/1.1

### HTTP/2
GET https://httpbin.org/anything HTTP/2

### A header value continues on an indented line
GET https://httpbin.org/anything
X-Long-Header: first part,
  second part

### Non-ASCII and emoji in the URL are percent-encoded for you
GET https://httpbin.org/anything/café?q=日本語&emoji=🚀

### @no-auto-encoding sends the URL exactly as written (already encoded here)
# @no-auto-encoding
GET https://httpbin.org/anything/caf%C3%A9?q=a%2Bb

### Comment lines in a body are not sent, and \{{ sends a literal {{
POST https://httpbin.org/anything
Content-Type: text/plain

Dear \{{name}}, this line is sent with its braces.
# This line is a comment: it is not sent.
// Nor is this one.
The last line is sent.

### Not supported: reported, and not sent
GRAPHQL https://httpbin.org/anything

### Nor are these
WEBSOCKET wss://echo.websocket.org

###
GRPC grpcb.in:9000/grpcbin.GRPCBin/Index
